{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he called.</b> The correct reading: \"the daughters of death,\" for you reversed my command. And there is no difference between ותאמרנה עבר (a form meaning 'you [f.pl.] spoke'), like ותאכלנה הפרות (Genesis 41:4), and when he speaks to them face to face, by introducing the vav with open [shva] — and likewise: 'Why did you do this, that you let them live?'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma ויקרא is the opening word of Exod. 1:18; Ibn Ezra's grammatical point concerns whether the feminine plural suffix-form ותאמרנה is second person ('you said') or third person ('they said'). The phrase 'בנות מות' ('daughters of death') is obscure as it stands; rendered hyper-literally. Possibly a textual corruption for בשות מות or similar."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:57.194407779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}